h1('2. Architecture and ownership')
bullets(['The existing application is a vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript workspace. app.js owns the live state and native rendering; zorifi-* modules extend it. No disconnected Vanessa demo or second editor state store was added.','Frontend hosting uses the existing Vercel workflow. Same-origin Node API wrappers route into shared backend modules; older Netlify wrappers are retained.','Firebase Authentication supplies real account identity. Server routes verify bearer tokens; emulator identity is restricted to explicit local demo projects.','Studio project metadata and original media remain device-local: account-scoped local storage and IndexedDB owner/project/asset records. Social sharing and assistant conversation records have separate, explicit cloud paths.','The native project history captures clips and creator settings. Media sources stay available for Undo/Redo and reopening; asynchronous jobs must separately manage staged media.','Vanessa proposals are structured data: interpretation, schema validation, scope/ownership checks, review when needed, native API, postcondition verification, history and persistence. Model text is never arbitrary code execution.'])
